.TH WEBWG-SERVER 1 "October 2026" "webwg 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webwg-server \- web admin for WireGuard servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webwg-server
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webwg-server
runs WireGuard servers on this machine and serves a web page where admins
approve devices, add peers and hand out their configs. Devices ask to join
from its join page, where their keys are made in the browser, or with the
.B cliwg.py
client it serves.
.PP
It manages WireGuard interfaces over netlink, so it needs root or
CAP_NET_ADMIN. The packaged service runs it as the
.B webwg
user with only that capability, from
.IR /var/lib/webwg .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-ini " \fIpath\fR"
Read an additional ini file.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " \fIaddress\fR"
Address to listen on, 127.0.0.1 by default.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
Port to listen on, 9999 by default.
.TP
.B \-\-sqlite\-migrate
Apply schema changes that cannot lose data to the database at startup. Without it
webwg stops and lists the changes when the database is out of date.
.TP
.BI \-\-dblogin\-add\-user " user password"
Create a user, or set the password of an existing one, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dblogin\-list\-users
List the users and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-nginx " \fR[\fIserver_name\fR]"
Install an nginx site for webwg.
.TP
.BI \-\-systemd " \fR[\fIuser\fR]"
Install a systemd service for webwg. Not needed with the package, which
ships its own.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-debug
Log verbose debugging information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/webwg/webwg.ini
Settings that override the defaults shipped with webwg, including the
database path.
.TP
.I /var/lib/webwg/webwg.db
The database of servers, peers, requests, users and sessions.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create the first admin user for the packaged service:
.PP
.EX
sudo \-u webwg webwg\-server \-\-dblogin\-add\-user admin 'password'
.EE
